`getSubmittedDate` and `getApprovedDate` (added just above) are nearly identical — both scan `actions` for the extreme `created` timestamp of a single action type, differing only in the action-type constant and their status guard. `getFirstApprovedAction` reimplements the same loop a third time, and this exact "scan actions, pick earliest/latest by `new Date(action.created).getTime()`" pattern already appears elsewhere in this file (e.g. around lines 1457, 1807, and 1817 for exported/approved actions). Adding three more copies increases the duplication and maintenance burden.

