The pattern of building an optimistic snapshot update (calling `buildCannedSearchQuery`, then `buildSearchQueryJSON`, then pushing a merge update to `ONYXKEYS.COLLECTION.SNAPSHOT`) is duplicated between `src/libs/actions/Report/index.ts` and `src/libs/actions/Task.ts`. This increases maintenance overhead -- if the snapshot update structure changes, both locations must be updated.

Consider extracting a shared helper function, for example:

```typescript
// In a shared utility (e.g., SearchUtils.ts or ReportUtils.ts)
function buildOptimisticSnapshotData(
    type: string,
    data: Record<string, unknown>,
): OnyxUpdate | undefined {
    const searchQuery = buildCannedSearchQuery({type});
    const searchQueryJSON = buildSearchQueryJSON(searchQuery);
    if (\!searchQueryJSON) {
        return undefined;
    }
    return {
        onyxMethod: Onyx.METHOD.MERGE,
        key: `${ONYXKEYS.COLLECTION.SNAPSHOT}${searchQueryJSON.hash}`,
        value: {data},
    };
}
```

Then both `Report/index.ts` and `Task.ts` can call `buildOptimisticSnapshotData()` instead of duplicating the query-building and snapshot-pushing logic.

