**Duplicated logic:** The pattern of wrapping text nodes with `aria-hidden` on web appears in both `renderPhrasingChildren` (lines 43-52) and the main `TNodeChildrenRenderer` (lines 111-120).

**Suggested fix:** Extract the common logic into a reusable helper function:

```tsx
function renderTextWithAccessibility(
    props: { key: string; childElement: React.ReactNode; childTnode: TNode },
    isWeb: boolean,
    tagStyle: TextStyle,
) {
    const isLink = props.childTnode.tagName === 'a';

    // On web, hide non-link text from accessibility tree
    if (isWeb && !isLink && props.childTnode.type === 'text') {
        return (
            <Text key={props.key} aria-hidden style={tagStyle}>
                {props.childElement}
            </Text>
        );
    }

    return props.childElement;
}

// Then use it in both places:
renderChild={(props) => renderTextWithAccessibility(props, isWeb, tagStyle)}
```

